WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.448 --> 00:00:02.662
- [Narrator] Mitchell
Kriegman created the show

00:00:02.662 --> 00:00:04.378
Clarissa Explains It All.

00:00:04.378 --> 00:00:05.595
- Yeah, I did.

00:00:05.595 --> 00:00:07.512
- [Narrator] And some other classics.

00:00:07.512 --> 00:00:09.283
- Yeah, I created Bear
In The Big Blue House,

00:00:09.283 --> 00:00:10.962
and I worked on Rugrats, Ren And Stimpy,

00:00:10.962 --> 00:00:11.962
Doug, Rocko.

00:00:12.939 --> 00:00:15.331
- [Narrator] But, I love
Clarissa, so we came out here

00:00:15.331 --> 00:00:16.648
to talk about it,

00:00:16.648 --> 00:00:18.724
and learn some things about
the show that we probably

00:00:18.724 --> 00:00:20.271
didn't know.

00:00:20.271 --> 00:00:21.508
- Cool.

00:00:21.508 --> 00:00:23.508
- [Narrator] Here we go.

00:00:25.575 --> 00:00:28.202
- The ladder was, I
think, about four rungs,

00:00:28.202 --> 00:00:29.048
or something like that.

00:00:29.048 --> 00:00:31.711
It was like about maybe this high,

00:00:31.711 --> 00:00:35.094
and Sam had to crouch
down underneath the window

00:00:35.094 --> 00:00:36.615
and go like a mime, you know,

00:00:36.615 --> 00:00:38.488
coming up every time,

00:00:38.488 --> 00:00:39.944
and he had to slam it on there,

00:00:39.944 --> 00:00:43.584
we had to get that guitar
sting in, of course,

00:00:43.584 --> 00:00:46.847
and when they built the set
you could see in the pilot,

00:00:46.847 --> 00:00:48.524
we eventually fixed this, right?

00:00:48.524 --> 00:00:50.709
In the pilot, you can
see through the window

00:00:50.709 --> 00:00:53.126
and see the floor of the studio.

00:00:56.027 --> 00:00:59.937
I banned purple, I would
never give a reason,

00:00:59.937 --> 00:01:02.922
and I kinda rationalized
it a little bit by saying,

00:01:02.922 --> 00:01:04.641
yeah I'm trying to
appeal to boys and girls,

00:01:04.641 --> 00:01:06.835
and I said, well it's gotta
be all pink and blue,

00:01:06.835 --> 00:01:08.187
you know, we gotta use
those as our main colors,

00:01:08.187 --> 00:01:09.880
and purple throws that off.

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:13.152
Bullshit, you know,
complete bullshit, right?

00:01:13.152 --> 00:01:16.069
They just ignored me after a while.

00:01:18.588 --> 00:01:21.982
Well, I can't really tell
you is the problem with that,

00:01:21.982 --> 00:01:25.482
and I've never told anybody, even Melissa.

00:01:26.936 --> 00:01:28.572
I had the most amazing writers.

00:01:28.572 --> 00:01:31.110
I had Suzanne Collins
who wrote Hunger Games,

00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:33.886
Alexa Junge, who was was one
of the main writers on Friends,

00:01:33.886 --> 00:01:36.594
Neena Beber wrote plays and wrote Daria.

00:01:36.594 --> 00:01:38.348
I mean, these writers, you know,

00:01:38.348 --> 00:01:42.265
all went on to do like
amazing stuff, you know?

00:01:44.172 --> 00:01:47.005
If you're like 26 to 36, you know,

00:01:48.018 --> 00:01:50.714
almost universally, if I say I created

00:01:50.714 --> 00:01:52.273
Clarissa Explains It All,

00:01:52.273 --> 00:01:55.651
they scream like a 14 year old girl,

00:01:55.651 --> 00:01:56.940
and they say that's my childhood,

00:01:56.940 --> 00:01:57.810
you made my childhood,

00:01:57.810 --> 00:02:00.424
and those are the words everybody says.

00:02:00.424 --> 00:02:02.542
It's like my career is 30
years younger than I am,

00:02:02.542 --> 00:02:04.359
you know, which I love.

00:02:04.359 --> 00:02:09.149
It's super satisfying,
it's completely wonderful.

00:02:09.149 --> 00:02:13.149
♫ Just do it ♫

